Foreword 
The 2024 National Population Census Final Figures booklet is a quick and easy way of informing 
everyone about the population of their own areas. These numbers have been finalized after 
extensive checking and editing were carried out. 
Data collectors visited 30,419 geographical census units to collect the census data. The total 
persons that were counted during the census period, starting from Sunday 16th June to October 
2024 was 10,185,363. This includes the Autonomous Region of Bougainville.  
Some findings are;
PNG T otal Population 10, 185,363 
PNG T otal Male Population    5,336,546  
PNG T otal Female Population    4,848,817  
Southern Regional Population    2,320,205  
Highlands Regional Population    3,634,114 
Momase Regional Population    2,753,211  
Islands Regional Population    1,477 ,833 
PNG average annual Growth Rate (2011 - 2024)     2.6%  
Southern Regional average Annual Growth Rate (2011 - 2024)    3.6% 
Highlands Regional Average Annual Growth Rate (2011 - 2024)     1.9% 
Momase Regional Average Annual Growth Rate (2011 – 2024)         3.0% 
Islands Regional Average Annual Growth Rate (2011 - 2024)    2.3%  
PNG Crude Population Density per square kilometre       22 persons
The 2024 Census information is a direct response to rapid growth in the demand for population 
and demographic data, particularly at lower levels of planning. This has been reinforced by the 
Organic Law on devolving specific responsibilities from the National Government to the  
provinces, districts, and local governments; civil registration of citizens; and progressing the  
electoral reforms. 
The NSO is indebted to the Government of Papua New Guinea for the funding of the 2024  
National Population Census Project. 
October 2025  
 
John Aseavu Igitoi       Hajily Kele 
National Statistician       Census Director

