Preface
2024 Census Final Figures
This report presents the final figures from the 2024 National Population Census for Papua New 
Guinea (PNG). Figures for each region, province, and district are included. 
Census information in this report represents only a selection of topics from the Census. Detailed 
demographic information from the 2024 Census will be released progressively. Detailed analytical 
reports and other products will follow.
The figures in this report show where people were counted at the time of the census. Visitors were 
included at their location at the time of counting. Census reference night was Sunday 16th June 
2024; however, counting extended over to October because of the communication and transport 
difficulties in doing such a large–scale exercise covering the whole country.
The National Statistical Office (NSO) acknowledges the full support of the government of PNG and 
UNFPA, the US Census Bureau, as well as many organizations and individuals who contributed to the 
planning and conduct of the Census. Most of all, we thank the people of PNG for their cooperation 
and participation in this important national event.

3
1. PAPUA NEW GUINEA OVERVIEW
 
Papua New Guinea’s population has passed the 10 million mark. The 2024 National Population   
Census counted 10,185,363 people in PNG on Census night.
This represents an increase of 40% (2,910,039 people) in PNG’s population count since 2011 
(7 ,275,324)
The average annual growth rate over the past 13 years, since the 2011 Census, was 2.6%.
Annual growth rate since the 2011 Census is higher (3.1%) but is likely to be artificially inflated 
because of non-demographic factors such as higher undercounting in 2000 and improvements to 
the 2011 and 2024 Census coverage methods.
More males than females were counted in PNG on Census night (52.4% and 47 .6% of the total 
population, respectively). This represents approximately 110 males to every 100 females.
The average number of people per household was 5 for PNG.
Since the first official census in 1980, five years after independence, there have been an additional 
7 .2 million people added from 3.0 million in the last 44 years
